# Learn more https://docs.github.com/en/get-started/getting-started-with-git/ignoring-files

# dependencies
node_modules/

# Expo
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
expo-env.d.ts

# Native
.kotlin/
*.orig.*
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision

# Metro
.metro-health-check*

# debug
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*

# macOS
.DS_Store
*.pem

# local env files
.env*.local
# ...and the plain one, which the Expo template does NOT cover. Publishable
# keys live in app.config.ts -> extra and are meant to ship; a provider key in
# .env is not, and a repo going public cannot rely on nobody running
# `git add -A`.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo

# generated native folders
/ios
/android

# Gradle output from the local Expo module. `modules/ridik-widgets/android/` is
# source, but Gradle writes its build tree inside it — 156 files of dex, caches
# and jars that were committed once by an over-broad `git add -A`.
modules/*/android/build/

# The Android upload key and its passwords. A signing key in version control is
# the one credential you cannot rotate — every past release is signed with it
# and Play will not accept a different one.
credentials/

# Release artefacts: `npm run release` writes the APK, AAB, archive and IPA here.
dist/

# Skill caches fetched by editor plugins (Stripe's, currently). Vendored copies
# of somebody else's documentation, re-fetched on demand and pinned by a lock
# file that records a remote digest — committing them would put a third party's
# docs in this repo's history and diff them on every refresh.
.agents/
.bob/
.claude/skills/
skills-lock.json

# Scratch git worktrees created for isolated parallel work.
.claude/worktrees/

# A personal working list, not a document the repo ships. Kept beside the code
# so it is read, and out of history so it can be edited without a commit.
BACKLOG.txt

# An exit plan for a dependency, not a document the repo ships. Kept beside the
# code so it is found when it is needed, and out of history so it can be
# rewritten as the coupling changes.
REMOVING-ONESIGNAL.md

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Anything an agent writes that is not the product.
#
# This repository is public. Working notes, audits, research write-ups, plans,
# migration checklists and exit strategies are all genuinely useful and none of
# them are things a stranger reading the source should have to wade through —
# several also name prices, keys by variable, or plans that have not been
# decided yet.
#
# The rule for every future agent, stated in AGENTS.md as well so it is read
# before it is broken: **a file that is not shipped code, shipped docs or a
# test goes in `notes/`.** It is kept beside the code so it is found when it is
# needed, and out of history so it can be rewritten without a commit.
#
# BACKLOG.txt and REMOVING-ONESIGNAL.md above predate the convention and are
# named individually rather than moved, because both are referenced by name in
# conversations and in AGENTS.md.
/notes/

# Scratch tests an agent writes to reproduce a bug and then forgets to remove.
# Two of these reached a commit during the August audits. A repro case is a
# good thing to write and a bad thing to ship: it is named for the bug rather
# than the behaviour, and it fails as soon as the bug is fixed.
**/__tests__/zz*.test.ts
**/__tests__/zz*.test.tsx

# local-only agent notes (full working notes live in notes/)
CLAUDE.local.md
